From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:54:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/34] D3D11 frame recording through a deferred context
 (FFXII_D3D_RECORD=1)

The game's immediate-context calls go to a host deferred context; the list
runs on the immediate context at sync points: Present, ResizeBuffers,
GetData, Flush and maps that read. The first NO_OVERWRITE map of a buffer
in a list becomes a DISCARD refilled from a host mirror of the buffer, as
deferred contexts require. This is the base for replaying a frame with
blended constant buffers. FFXII field and combat render identically and
hold 60 fps with it on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
